9. THE MODEL - VOCABULARY FIXED 2026-09-30

boundary loop   - a closed sequence of 3D points.
anchor          - a point where two segments meet.
segment         - the gap between two anchors.
segment type    - beam, cable, or wall.
held            - a mesh node solve_fdm does not move.
released        - a mesh node solve_fdm moves to
                  equilibrium.
fabric edge     - how the membrane attaches along a
                  segment.
Kader Guider    - continuous attachment. No bow.
Cable Supported - discrete attachment at anchors. Bows.
Edge Cable Pretension (kN) - the fabric edge cable value.
Tie-down Pretension (kN)   - the ground tie-down cable
                             value. Default 2.5 kN.

Words retired forever:
  free end, short end, long edge, free edge,
  column at support, degenerate column.

The hold rule:
  Anchor                  -> always held.
  Segment interior, beam  -> held.
  Segment interior, wall  -> held.
  Segment interior, cable -> released.
  Interior mesh nodes     -> always released.

